explain_text() {
    local cmd="${1:-help}"
    case "$cmd" in
        adderall)
            cat <<'EOF'
adderall — the everything command.
  1. Installs missing build tools AUTOMATICALLY (clang, dpkg, THEOS,
     libimobiledevice) — zero questions
  2. Finds your phone over USB or WiFi and pairs it (tap TRUST on the phone)
     — when the phone is on USB, a USB SSH tunnel (iproxy) is started and
     deploys go over USB, no WiFi IP needed. --usb forces USB-only.
  3. Tests the USB cable (10 rapid reads — warns if it's flaky)
  4. Checks your iOS version is supported by the offset table
  5. Compiles the tweak ON THIS COMPUTER (Theos + clang)
  6. Copies the .deb to the phone and installs it (needs OpenSSH on the phone)
  7. Restarts Filza and waits ~12s while the kernel exploit runs
  8. Reads the phone's log and tells you if the sandbox escaped

  It does NOT install Filza (you sideload that yourself), and it does
  NOT jailbreak the phone (that must already be done). Everything it
  does is undone by a reboot. Safe mode (--safe) skips the exploit.
EOF
            ;;
        deploy)
            cat <<'EOF'
deploy — install an already-built tweak onto the phone.
  Takes the newest .deb from packages/, copies it over SSH, installs it
  with dpkg, and restarts Filza. Does not build — run 'build' first if
  you changed code. Filza must already be installed on the phone.
EOF
            ;;
        build)
            cat <<'EOF'
build — compile the tweak ON THIS COMPUTER.
  Runs Theos (make package) to produce a .deb in packages/. Nothing is
  sent to the phone. If this fails, run 'doctor' to see which tool is
  missing, or 'sudo ./W0lfSword setup' to install them all.
EOF
            ;;
        safe)
            cat <<'EOF'
safe — the safety switch.
  'safe on' puts a flag file on the phone. Next time Filza opens, the
  tweak loads its UI hooks (padlock/license bypass) but skips ALL kernel
  writes — nothing risky happens. 'safe off' removes the flag so the
  real exploit runs again. Always test new devices in safe mode first.
EOF
            ;;
        toggle)
            cat <<'EOF'
toggle — remote kill-switch.
  'toggle on' creates a flag file on the phone that makes the tweak do
  nothing at all (no hooks, no exploit). 'toggle off' re-enables it.
  Use this instead of uninstalling when you want to pause.
EOF
            ;;
        quick)
            cat <<'EOF'
quick — one button, build + deploy + verify.
  Same as 'build' then 'deploy' then waiting for the exploit and
